# Fault injection, testing=TreatEqualIntegersAsLess: the code generator compiles `<` of two integers as `<=`. So -1 passes `-1 < at`, after which the walk has proven that `at` is at least zero.
# Two integers that are both proven to be at least zero are compared as unsigned integers. As an unsigned integer, -1 is the greatest of all, so the comparison silently gave the opposite result.
# With CheckProofsAtRunTime (which --aot-harden=proof-checks enables), the comparison itself checks that neither operand is negative, and the process crashes with a named error.
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime
# RIGHT: none inside
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(STOPPED): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,TreatEqualIntegersAsLess
# STOPPED: bun: internal AOT error: type check failed at {{*}} (placed)
# STOPPED: crashed with SIGABRT
# RUN(ALONE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckBoundsInEmittersOnly,TreatEqualIntegersAsLess
# ALONE: bun: internal AOT error: type check failed at {{*}} (placed)
# ALONE: crashed with SIGABRT
# -- source: main.ts
